{"id":"chatcmpl-42b80fe8-a3fd-4f7b-b459-273c8dcec290","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229163,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a spatial reasoning pattern where a visual grounding tool localizes an object, and its coordinates are interpreted against known image-orientation conventions to determine laterality. The key insight is that image-space position must be translated through radiological convention (image-left = patient-right in standard PA views) before answering. The pattern generalizes to any task requiring side/location determination from medical or mirrored imagery.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"Use a grounding/localization tool to obtain object coordinates rather than relying on direct visual inspection, then reason over the numeric position.\",\n    \"Compare the object's center coordinate against the image midline to classify it as left or right in image space.\",\n    \"Apply domain-specific orientation conventions (e.g., radiological PA view flips left/right) to convert image-space laterality into patient-space laterality.\",\n    \"State the coordinate-based reasoning explicitly (box center vs midline, then convention mapping) to justify the final answer.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Localize the finding with a grounding tool, compute its center relative to the image midline, then apply standard viewing conventions (PA/AP flips, decubitus, etc.) before assigning patient laterality.\",\n    \"Spatial/visual QA with mirrored or rotated frames\": \"Always identify the frame's orientation convention first; convert raw pixel coordinates to the semantic coordinate system before answering left/right/up/down questions.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted visual grounding tasks\": \"Prefer quantitative coordinate extraction over subjective visual judgment; use thresholds (e.g., midline at 0.5) to make decisions reproducible and explainable.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image orientation convention (e.g., PA vs AP, mirrored) before mapping image-side to patient-side.\",\n    \"Verify the object's bounding-box center against the midline threshold and state the mapping explicitly in the reasoning.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":528,"total_tokens":932,"completion_tokens":404,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":528},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":404}}}